# Phoenix is a framework. Its inputs are the developer's code and config, not request data.
# DOS.BinToAtom:        atoms are built at compile time from route, controller and module names.
# DOS.StringToAtom:     atoms come from route path param names, generator CLI arguments and
#                       module file names. None comes from request values.
# RCE.EEx:              EEx runs only generator templates from priv/templates of Phoenix or of
#                       the app, when a developer runs mix phx.gen.*.
# Traversal.FileModule: File calls work on paths from config, build output and generator
#                       arguments. Request paths never reach them.
# Config.HTTPS:         kept as the Glia standard asks. Phoenix is a library, so TLS is set
#                       by the application that uses it.
# XSS.SendResp, Traversal.SendFile, XSS.ContentType, CI.System: handled with annotations
#                       next to each call, each with a reason.
[
  skip: true,
  private: true,
  router: :none,
  ignore: [
    "Config.HTTPS",
    "DOS.BinToAtom",
    "DOS.StringToAtom",
    "RCE.EEx",
    "Traversal.FileModule"
  ]
]
